message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  A Latch-On-Resistant, False-Alarm-Gated Lead-Time Metric for Bearing
  Anomaly Detection — and What It Reveals About SCADA-Rate Logging
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ansh
    family-names: Goyal
    affiliation: "Jaypee Institute of Information Technology, Noida, India"
    email: anshgoyal5500@gmail.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # add your ORCID, then uncomment
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ansh-Goyal01/Scada-Leadtime-Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Code, result files and manuscript source accompanying the IJPHM manuscript
  'A Latch-On-Resistant, False-Alarm-Gated Lead-Time Metric for Bearing
  Anomaly Detection — and What It Reveals About SCADA-Rate Logging'. The
  benchmark scores bearing anomaly detectors by lead time gated on a pre-onset
  false-alarm budget, and tests whether a SCADA historian's bin-averaged
  logging changes warning time relative to decimation, across four
  run-to-failure datasets (XJTU-SY, FEMTO/PRONOSTIA, University of Ferrara,
  NASA IMS) and one industrial case study. On the three multi-bearing
  campaigns the aggregate-minus-decimate difference is equivalent to zero
  within a pre-specified ±1 h margin; because those bearings are short-lived,
  the result bounds the effect at the scale of minutes. Every table and figure
  is generated from results/tables/ and checked by paper/verify_tables.py.
keywords:
  - predictive maintenance
  - prognostics and health management
  - lead time
  - anomaly detection
  - condition monitoring
  - rolling-element bearing
  - SCADA
  - conformal prediction
  - statistical process control
